# Official Qwen Qwen3.8-27B, unquantized BF16 (full precision). Same architecture as
# qwen3.8-27b-fp8 / -nvfp4: dense 27.8B hybrid Gated-DeltaNet + full-attention, vision, native 256K
# context, 1 native MTP layer. Highest-fidelity sibling; the slowest, because decode on GB10 is
# bandwidth-bound and BF16 weights are ~2x the FP8 bytes (~54 GB vs ~30.9 GB).
#
# DRAFT, 2026-11-10: restored as the new default (an earlier BF16 recipe was removed 2026-09-02) and
# NOT YET VALIDATED on vLLM v0.33.0 (stack bumped from v0.31.0 the same day). Before clearing EXPERIMENTAL, run on the box:
#   1. Load it, then run the swap-ui stability battery.
#   2. MTP sweep (no-spec / k=3 / k=4), with the 32-trial strict tool gate, as for -fp8 / -nvfp4.
#   3. MMLU via lm_eval loglikelihood. The -fp8 sweep scored 0.853 at k=4. Spec-decode has
#      corrupted logprob scoring on this family before (v0.27/0.28), so check it, not just tok/s.
# Expected decode with no spec, scaled from -fp8's 8.07 tok/s by weight bytes: roughly 4-5 tok/s
# single-stream. The 2026-08-16 "~16.5 tok/s" figure on the old BF16 recipe is not credible at
# BF16 bandwidth on this box; re-measure instead of trusting it.
#
# Checked 2026-11-10 against the official vLLM recipe (vllm-project/recipes
# models/Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B.yaml, updated 2026-10-15; dgx_spark_gb10 = verified). For the BF16
# variant on GB10 it sets --max-num-seqs 8 and --gpu-memory-utilization 0.8, both adopted here.
# VERSION MISMATCH: the recipe's GB10 runs used vllm/vllm-openai:qwen38 (0.1.dev19754+g3a0914114,
# a dev build) with the Rust frontend (VLLM_USE_RUST_FRONTEND=1). That is neither our pinned
# release nor our frontend: gb10-serve.sh runs the Python frontend. No version-matched GB10 guidance
# exists for v0.33.0, so these settings are "documented, unverified on our version" until the
# battery + MMLU pass here.
# max-num-seqs 8 also avoids the "max_num_seqs exceeds available Mamba cache blocks" startup error.
# The GDN spec-decode fixes the recipe asks for (vllm#51812, #51674) and the MTP acceptance-
# collapse fix (#59309) all merged before v0.31.0 (released 2026-10-05), so v0.33.0 has them too.
#
# Policy (2026-11-10): follow the documented vLLM recipe over older local guidance.
# Spec-decode: MTP k=5, the recipe's dgx_spark_gb10 override (BF16 short-prompt acceptance 92%).
# Caveat to watch: open vllm#63593 reports MTP divergence from the target model at k>=5 on this
# model; run the MMLU check before clearing EXPERIMENTAL.
# Tool parser: qwen3_coder, the recipe default (also NVIDIA's card). This overrides
# gb10-serve.sh's qwen3_xml default, which came from a 2026-07 Qwen3.6-era finding. The recipe
# switched because qwen3_xml breaks on the Rust frontend (vllm-project/recipes#1086). On the Python
# frontend both parse Qwen3.8's <function=...> format, and on v0.32.0+ Rust treats qwen3_xml as an
# alias of qwen3_coder (#60136).
# Default cudagraph mode: v0.31.0's Model Runner V2 no longer needs PIECEWISE forcing.
# KV_ARG="" -> auto, which resolves to bf16 for a BF16 checkpoint (the auto->fp8 bug only affects
# ModelOpt/NVFP4 checkpoints).
# Sampling: GENCFG_ARG="" serves the checkpoint's generation_config.json (temp 1.0, top_p 0.95,
# top_k 20), which matches the model card's thinking-mode recommendation.
# Prefix caching: gb10-serve.sh always passes --enable-prefix-caching. vllm#48375 (prefix caching +
# MTP on hybrid GDN reusing a snapshot with rejected draft tokens) is unmerged, but v0.32/v0.33
# landed the Mamba-checkpoint + MTP + prefix-caching fixes (#59759, #60797, #61589). Still watch
# multi-turn output quality.

# --- UI metadata ---
UI_LABEL="Qwen3.8-27B"
UI_DESC="Official Qwen3.8-27B, unquantized BF16 (full precision), with native MTP speculative decoding (k=5, per the vLLM GB10 recipe). Highest-fidelity sibling of qwen3.8-27b-fp8/-nvfp4, and the slowest of the three. ~54 GB, native 256K context, vision. Draft: not yet validated on vLLM v0.33.0."
UI_SIZE="~54 GB · BF16 unquantized · vision · 256K ctx"
UI_SPEED="~25.4 tok/s (measured 2026-11-10)"
UI_USE_CASES="Vision Q&A, Long-context (256K) reading, Agentic tool-use, Max-fidelity reference"
EXPERIMENTAL="0"

# --- Serve recipe ---
SERVE_MODEL="Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B"
SERVED_NAME="qwen3.8-27b"
SERVE_CONTAINER="swap-vllm-qwen3.8-27b"
SERVE_PORT="8002"
MAX_LEN="262144"
GPU_UTIL="0.8"
QUANT="auto"
TOOLS="1"
REASONING_PARSER="qwen3"
TOOL_PARSER="qwen3_coder"
KV_ARG=""
GENCFG_ARG=""
EXTRA_ARGS="--max-num-seqs 8 --max-num-batched-tokens 8192 --performance-mode interactivity"
SPEC_ARG="--speculative-config '{\"method\":\"mtp\",\"num_speculative_tokens\":5}'"
COMPILE_ARG=""
# ~54 GB of BF16 weights plus compile/cudagraph capture. -nvfp4 already needed ~930s, past the
# 900s default health wait (see swapper #33).
SERVE_TIMEOUT="1500"
